{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_introspection_shards", "label": "shards(typeName)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The coordinator owns the shard map but not the entity counts, so the call fans out to every registered region and joins against the allocation map; the deadline is a partial-answer deadline - a slow or departed region contributes entityCount 0 rather than failing the call. Shards with no home yet are absent, since nothing has asked for them.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/introspection.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_introspection_shardinfo", "label": "ShardInfo", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Carries a live ref rather than only placement data, so one query answers both what is out there and how to talk to it; the trade-off is that it is not JSON-serialisable, and it is a snapshot - entityCount was true when the region answered and node holds only until the next rebalance.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/introspection.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_introspection_shardreffor", "label": "shardRefFor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Places a homeless shard exactly as a first message would. The ref carries the shard's path as identity from any node; what changes is the route - direct when local, through the owning region when not - so a local call wakes a passivated shard and a remote one is woken by the first tell. ask on a remote shard ref times out because the synthesised reply ref has no place in the far node's actor tree.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/introspection.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_introspection_entityreffor", "label": "entityRefFor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The handle names its entity, so extractEntityId is never consulted and the message needs no routing key; synchronous to obtain because the shard is hash(entityId) % numShards. ask works wherever the entity lives because the region forwards the sender, and a proxy region is enough to hand one out.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/introspection.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_introspection_shardmapchanged", "label": "ShardMapChanged", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Fires on every node, not just the leader - the coordinator broadcasts to each region and the region publishes locally - which is what makes it usable from an application listener or per-node dashboard. Broadcasts are coalesced, so version counts broadcasts and not shards moved.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/introspection.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_introspection_resident", "label": "ShardInfo.resident flag", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Separates a shard that is running and happens to be empty from one that passivated while empty - entityCount 0 reports both; it does not affect whether the ref works, and is read when tuning shardPassivationIdleMs or counting the actors a node really holds.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/sharding/introspection.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_introspection_shards", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_sharding_introspection_shardinfo", "relation": "references", "confidence"